From: mlgprorektm8 <67933lance@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 06:34:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] In-game Controllers window and 2 controller ports

- F3, or holding Share/View + Options/Menu on a controller for 0.6 s, opens a Controllers window
  over the game in the launcher's style: which controller plays as player 1 and player 2
  changes at once, without a restart, and is saved to Input.controller_ports for the launcher
  and the next start. The game gets released controls while it is open; it scales with the
  game's resolution.
- Its live preview draws the controller in use: DualShock 4 (coloured symbols, light bar),
  DualSense (white, light strips) or Xbox (offset sticks, coloured A/B/X/Y); other controllers
  get the Xbox layout without colours. The light bar and strips show the game's colour.
- 2 controller ports (Split Screen is for 2 players): the input bridge forwards 2 players, gamepads
  go into 2 ports, a gamepad without a free port is closed again, and events of a gamepad without
  a port are ignored. Ports are reassigned live through SDL_EVENT_CHANGE_CONTROLLER.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
